+#### `rg -n 'TODO|FIXME|XXX|window\.confirm|window\.prompt|window\.alert|eslint-disable' extension/src/review -S`
+
+Result: exit code `1`, meaning no matches were found.
+
+## Issues encountered
+
+- The review panel is still an inline webview running under the extension's CommonJS build, so the new queue/dialog modules could not be loaded as normal browser imports. The fix was to serialize the browser-side function bundles into the existing inline webview script and add a provider-side RPC request/response bridge for queue actions.
+- `reviewPanel.ts` already contained partially integrated Phase 10 route state and helper blocks. The first compile surfaced duplicated/missing helper paths in that file; those were cleaned up so the new queue routes could compile against the existing event-trace and retrieval-explanation scaffolding.
+- The promotion dialog required richer proposal detail than the existing `consolidate_session` review payload exposed. A narrow daemon integration fix was added so proposal rows now carry decision state, scopes, confidence, evidence count, before/after state, and provenance needed by the dialog.
+- The task file says to deploy after build, but the repo instructions require confirmation before restart/copy actions such as `pkill -f lattice` and copying binaries into the installed VS Code extension location. That deploy step was not run in this task result.
+
